    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nOwner deletion is now a soft-delete. Changes, kept as small additions in low-complexity spots:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `deleted` boolean field with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()` accessors (a new cohesive unit, no existing method touched).\n\n2. **`ClinicServiceImpl.deleteOwner`** \u2014 instead of removing the row, it now flags `deleted = true` and saves (the row is retained). CC-1 method, one line changed.\n\n3. **`OwnerIdentityUniquenessAspect`** and **`OwnerHouseholdDuplicateAdvice`** \u2014 the two blocking duplicate/identity checks each gained a single `.filter(existing -> !existing.isDeleted())`, so a soft-deleted owner no longer blocks a new create. Both live in tiny classes.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean (default `false`) to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it. GET now returns `deleted` (false for new owners, true after delete).\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql` / `data.sql`** \u2014 added the `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` column (the test profile uses `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema is authoritative) and appended `FALSE` to the seed inserts.\n\nThis satisfies the spec: DELETE returns 2xx and retains the record flagged deleted; GET still returns the owner with `deleted: true`; a newly created owner is `deleted: false`; and a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been soft-deleted (verified by `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck`).",
